report renders the operator_digest.v1 model for an explicit scope.

This first CLI implementation is an offline presentation path. It validates
share-safe input, emits deterministic unsupported sections, and points operators
to bounded follow-up routes without reading graph state, writing graph state,
claiming reducer work, or calling providers.

Usage:
  eshu report [flags]
  eshu report [command]

Available Commands:
  capture     Capture a share-safe wrong_answer_report.v1 bundle from a query
  validate    Validate a wrong_answer_report.v1 bundle

Flags:
      --artifact-out string   Write a shareable operator_digest_artifact.v1 JSON file
  -h, --help                  help for report
      --json                  Emit the digest as JSON
      --profile string        Runtime profile used to derive the digest (default "local_authoritative")
      --question-limit int    Maximum suggested questions to emit (0-25) (default 8)
      --scope string          Share-safe scope such as repo:owner/name, service:name, workload:name, environment:name, or project:name

Global Flags:
      --database string   Temporarily override database backend
  -V, --visual            Show results as interactive graph visualization

Use "eshu report [command] --help" for more information about a command.
